# EXPECT: shadows a module binding
#
# A `for` binder over a parameter that shadows a module name.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is a VM rule where the binder's post-loop
# persistence depends on a NON-LOCAL fact. Measured, the identical function:
#
#   define f(x) as: for x in [7, 8]: local q is x / return x
#   f of 1  ->  8   with no module x        (binder persists in the param)
#   f of 1  ->  1   with `x is 5` at module (binder loop-scoped)
#
# One C variable cannot express both halves, and the divergence predates the
# tape work entirely: the untraced form ran silently wrong (VM 1|5, AOT 8|5,
# both rc 0) for as long as the for-unboxing has existed. It surfaced only when
# a tape fixture happened to combine the shadow with a binder — two wrongs had
# coincided in the only shape anyone had tested.
#
# Sixth context-dependent scoping row sent to EigenScript#1056. The next
# review measured the rule to be GENERAL -- a function-body binder over any
# module-bound name loop-scopes (the plain-module-global row had been silently
# wrong since for-unboxing existed) -- so the guard now keys on module-bound-
# ness, not parameter-ness, and its sibling module_global_forbinder.eigs pins
# the row that was never a parameter at all.

x is 5

define f(x) as:
    for x in [7, 8]:
        local q is x
    return x

print of (f of 1)
print of x
